## Task 1: Implement Proxy-based Lazy Shallow Cloning (TDD)

**Files:** `services/store.js`, `tests/state.spec.js`

- [x] Write failing tests for Proxy-based state reads (O(1), no recursive cloning)
- [x] Write failing tests for structural sharing (unchanged objects maintain reference equality)
- [x] Write failing tests for Proxy-trapped property setting (clone only the modified path)
- [x] Write failing tests for subscriber notification on modification
- [x] Refactor `Store` class in `services/store.js` to use Proxy handler implementing Lazy Shallow Cloning per `06-RESEARCH.md`
- [x] Replace `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(this.state))` deep-clone with Proxy-based CoW
- [x] Ensure `getState()` returns a reactive snapshot or Proxy with efficient reads
- [x] Pass all tests — verify with `npm test tests/state.spec.js`
- [x] Confirm performance: O(1) read overhead demonstrated

**Done when:** Store uses structural sharing; performance tests show O(1) read overhead.

---

## Task 2: Segment State into Transient and Persistent

**Files:** `services/store.js`

- [x] Update `initialState` to separate `persistent` (rows, settings, theme) from `transient` (activeRowIndex, selection, focusState)
- [x] Ensure `saveToLocalStorage` only serializes the `persistent` segment
- [x] Implement `batch` update mechanism (multiple changes before notifying subscribers)
- [x] Verify segmentation: `grep "persistent" services/store.js && grep "transient" services/store.js`
- [x] Confirm transient state does not persist across page refreshes

**Done when:** State is segmented; LocalStorage only contains persistent data.

